Z||000000||Phoenix||04-14-2000||09:07 AM||||When I got my coupe a month ago, it came with a bunch of 87 parts (some I'll use some not).<BR>One item is a sunroof shade and the black cover for it. I don't have a sunsoof in my car so I don't need it.  Here's my question - is there a way to tell if it is a original cover or an aftermarket copy.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-14-2000||12:07 PM||||Just send it to me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'll tell you after if it fits.....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>I don't know if anyone made an after market one. I don't believe so. R.D.'s bag is not actually a fiero one, but you can also tell because it's too small. The only sure way to know it's at least the right size is to measure it. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phoenix||04-14-2000||12:18 PM||||The shade fits in the bag, does it mean it is a real one ?||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-14-2000||07:43 PM||||maybe. since you don't have the sunroof just measure the thing. someone here can check the number to be sure.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phoenix||04-15-2000||07:43 AM||||15&3/8" wide X 37" (to flap opening) 43" to end of flap.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodney||04-15-2000||12:41 PM||||Story on my reproduction sunshade bags is this: About a 2 years ago there was a large demand for sunshade bags and sunshades. But there were none for sale. I figured that most people did not really use them but wanted them to show of at shows. So I was able to find a used bag and copied it and made my reproduction bags. After I had did that I found that the bags shrink from the heat in the front compartment. So My bag is like the heat shrunk ones in size. It really should be larger. So I have about 50 of these small bags. So I sell them for owners that want to just cut some cardboard to stuff inside it and use it as a prop. It still looks correct in every way just too small to replace the OEM bag. Maybe someday if I sell all these I'll do another batch in the correct size.<P>Rodney Dickman||||reg||1
